1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,870
A customer books a cleaning.

2
00:00:02,080 --> 00:00:04,470
In the notes, they write,
"We have two cats."

3
00:00:04,880 --> 00:00:08,850
On the staff page, the app
says no pets, no pet fee,

4
00:00:09,020 --> 00:00:11,390
and it just sent the cleaner
who's allergic to cats.

5
00:00:11,920 --> 00:00:15,810
Ten minutes ago, I asked my AI to
remove one question from this form.

6
00:00:16,060 --> 00:00:17,330
It did exactly that.

7
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:21,190
It even warned me about part of this,
not the part that costs money.

8
00:00:21,480 --> 00:00:23,910
Let's look at what it saw,
what it couldn't see,

9
00:00:23,960 --> 00:00:27,070
and how to remove a field without
breaking the things that depend on it.

10
00:00:27,120 --> 00:00:29,670
Prompts and a check query are at the end.

11
00:00:35,460 --> 00:00:36,650
Here's the change.

12
00:00:36,980 --> 00:00:37,950
Two files.

13
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:39,590
The question is gone from the form,

14
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:42,110
and the line that saved
the answer is gone too.

15
00:00:42,760 --> 00:00:43,510
Clean.

16
00:00:43,560 --> 00:00:44,750
And it didn't stay quiet.

17
00:00:44,860 --> 00:00:47,810
It told me new bookings would
save the pets answer as blank.

18
00:00:48,220 --> 00:00:51,250
It told me the cleaner matching
treats blank as "no pets".

19
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:55,010
So a cleaner with a cat allergy
could get a home with pets,

20
00:00:55,100 --> 00:00:58,750
and the "Needs pet-friendly
cleaner" badge would stop showing.

21
00:00:59,080 --> 00:01:00,080
That's a good answer.

22
00:01:00,340 --> 00:01:02,930
Everything it mentioned was
true, but look at the price.

23
00:01:03,240 --> 00:01:05,110
This booking should be $165.

24
00:01:06,080 --> 00:01:09,970
$150 for two bedrooms, plus a $15 pet fee.

25
00:01:10,160 --> 00:01:12,970
The fee is gone, and the
AI never mentioned it.

26
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:16,790
So I searched the code.

27
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:19,250
The pet fee is displayed
on the staff page,

28
00:01:19,680 --> 00:01:21,750
but nothing in the code calculates it.

29
00:01:21,820 --> 00:01:23,230
It's calculated in the database.

30
00:01:23,560 --> 00:01:26,990
This query lists everything in the
database that uses the pets column.

31
00:01:27,320 --> 00:01:30,110
There's a view the staff page
reads, and there's a trigger,

32
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:32,150
a little function that
runs on every booking.

33
00:01:32,400 --> 00:01:35,310
Here it is. If the customer has pets, $15.

34
00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:37,150
Otherwise, zero.

35
00:01:37,620 --> 00:01:39,750
And "otherwise" includes "we never asked".

36
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:44,390
I put this pricing logic in the database
for this demo, but it's a common setup.

37
00:01:44,580 --> 00:01:47,090
Your AI tells you to paste
some SQL into the dashboard.

38
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:49,770
You do, and it never ends up in your code.

39
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,930
So when the AI searched my project,
there was nothing to find.

40
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:56,890
Its map of "where is this used"
stops at what it can read.

41
00:01:59,240 --> 00:02:03,650
So I gave it read access to the
database and asked the exact same thing.

42
00:02:03,940 --> 00:02:06,110
Fresh session, same prompt.

43
00:02:06,340 --> 00:02:07,550
This time it went further.

44
00:02:07,720 --> 00:02:10,250
Without asking, it changed
the cleaner matching.

45
00:02:10,740 --> 00:02:12,570
Unknown now means "might have pets",

46
00:02:12,860 --> 00:02:15,970
and the staff page shows
"Unknown" instead of "No".

47
00:02:16,040 --> 00:02:18,370
The cats booking goes to Ben now. Better.

48
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:20,210
But look at what that decision means.

49
00:02:20,540 --> 00:02:23,870
Ana, the cleaner with the
allergy, now gets no new jobs

50
00:02:23,920 --> 00:02:26,570
until someone on staff fills
in the pets answer by hand.

51
00:02:26,620 --> 00:02:28,450
That's a reasonable call.

52
00:02:28,580 --> 00:02:31,530
It's also a business decision
about your staff's work.

53
00:02:32,060 --> 00:02:35,170
The AI made it for you,
and the price is still $150.

54
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:37,190
It had access to the database.

55
00:02:37,720 --> 00:02:39,510
It didn't look at what uses the column.

56
00:02:39,800 --> 00:02:41,650
Having access isn't the same as checking.

57
00:02:42,140 --> 00:02:43,850
Which questions are yours to answer?

58
00:02:44,100 --> 00:02:45,370
I made a short about that.

59
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:46,730
It's linked in the description.

60
00:02:49,300 --> 00:02:50,890
Here's the core of the problem.

61
00:02:51,020 --> 00:02:53,630
Before, every booking said yes or no.

62
00:02:53,780 --> 00:02:55,510
Now new bookings say nothing.

63
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:56,690
Null.

64
00:02:56,740 --> 00:02:59,670
And every place that reads the
answer was written for yes or no.

65
00:02:59,760 --> 00:03:02,090
The staff page, the matching, the price.

66
00:03:02,480 --> 00:03:05,030
Each one treats "we didn't ask" as "no".

67
00:03:05,260 --> 00:03:07,350
"Remove the question"
sounds like one change.

68
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:07,950
It's four.

69
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:11,910
Stop asking, stop saving, stop using it.

70
00:03:11,960 --> 00:03:14,890
And decide what happens to
the answers you already have.

71
00:03:14,960 --> 00:03:18,110
The AI did the first two,
because that's what I asked for.

72
00:03:20,520 --> 00:03:22,870
So here's how to remove
a field without this.

73
00:03:22,980 --> 00:03:23,980
The order matters.

74
00:03:24,500 --> 00:03:25,510
One, decide.

75
00:03:25,720 --> 00:03:28,470
Are you dropping the information
or collecting it another way?

76
00:03:28,520 --> 00:03:29,690
What about the answers you have?

77
00:03:29,740 --> 00:03:33,030
For this business,
stop asking on the form.

78
00:03:33,420 --> 00:03:35,430
Staff confirm pets when
they confirm the booking.

79
00:03:35,980 --> 00:03:39,390
Keep the old answers, and no
pet fee until it's confirmed.

80
00:03:39,700 --> 00:03:42,150
Two, map out everything that uses it.

81
00:03:42,380 --> 00:03:45,750
Ask your AI for a full list,
and ask what it couldn't check.

82
00:03:45,900 --> 00:03:49,230
Then search the code yourself,
and run this query in your database.

83
00:03:49,760 --> 00:03:50,970
That's the one that finds the trigger.

84
00:03:51,020 --> 00:03:56,270
Three, make everything handle "unknown"
first, before you remove the question.

85
00:03:56,640 --> 00:04:00,870
Matching: only a confirmed no pets home
can go to a cleaner with an allergy.

86
00:04:01,320 --> 00:04:05,170
Staff page: "Unknown",
a "Confirm pets with customer" badge,

87
00:04:05,220 --> 00:04:09,030
and a dropdown so staff can
set yes, no, or unknown.

88
00:04:09,360 --> 00:04:10,790
The trigger can stay as it is.

89
00:04:11,160 --> 00:04:13,170
Unknown means no automatic
fee, which is our decision.

90
00:04:13,220 --> 00:04:15,970
And it reruns whenever
staff update the booking.

91
00:04:16,600 --> 00:04:18,550
Four, then remove the question.

92
00:04:18,680 --> 00:04:20,930
That's the part the AI already did.

93
00:04:21,200 --> 00:04:23,810
Five, drop the column later, or never.

94
00:04:24,040 --> 00:04:27,050
Here, we're keeping it,
because staff still record pets.

95
00:04:27,540 --> 00:04:30,650
If you do drop it, run the
dependency query first,

96
00:04:30,700 --> 00:04:33,590
and never add "cascade" just
to make an error go away.

97
00:04:36,420 --> 00:04:38,770
Don't trust the summary. Check it.

98
00:04:38,880 --> 00:04:40,690
Same booking process as the start.

99
00:04:44,160 --> 00:04:44,650
Unknown.

100
00:04:44,700 --> 00:04:45,730
Flagged for staff.

101
00:04:46,280 --> 00:04:47,750
Auto-assign skips Ana.

102
00:04:48,140 --> 00:04:49,390
Staff confirm the dog.

103
00:04:49,760 --> 00:04:50,930
The pet fee appears.

104
00:04:51,300 --> 00:04:52,300
$165.

105
00:04:52,780 --> 00:04:55,130
Old bookings keep their
answers, and everything

106
00:04:55,180 --> 00:04:57,550
the query found, you've
made a decision about.

107
00:05:00,060 --> 00:05:02,970
Before you remove any field, paste this.

108
00:05:03,100 --> 00:05:04,100
It's in the description.

109
00:05:13,940 --> 00:05:16,930
Then run this yourself in
the Supabase SQL editor.

110
00:05:17,180 --> 00:05:18,690
Change the table and column names.

111
00:05:18,940 --> 00:05:20,230
It's in the description too.

112
00:05:41,080 --> 00:05:43,210
The AI can find a lot of where.

113
00:05:43,320 --> 00:05:44,950
Make sure it can see everywhere.

114
00:05:45,120 --> 00:05:47,870
And decide what "remove"
means before it does.

